# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces current production (#4503): a routed write
# through a router that cached the purged old copy is accepted
# (PrepareForWriteAsync re-seeds a purged tree) and acknowledged, but lands on
# a copy the tree no longer resolves to, so the resized copy never holds it.
MODULE: NoKeyLostPurgedCopyAcceptsWrites
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a routed write on the purged old copy is accepted and acknowledged but lands where nothing reads it
PERTURBS: LaterWrite

--- FIND
       IN /\ ~RoutedRefused(c, s, k2)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the purged copy accepts the write.
       IN /\ ~RoutedRefused(c, s, k2) \/ Gone(c)
--- END
